The fix is complete. Here's what I did:

**Bug:** `extractTags(from:)` in `Sources/NoteKit/NoteKit.swift` split the text on whitespace and filtered tokens that started with `#`. This failed when a tag was attached to other characters — e.g. `"shopping list,#urgent."` produced `list,#urgent.` (no tag) and `"(#ideas)"` produced `(#ideas)` (no tag).

**Fix:** Replaced the split/filter/map approach with a regex scan (`#\w+`) that finds each `#` followed by word characters, collecting matches in order. This correctly extracts `#urgent` from `"shopping list,#urgent."` and `#ideas` from `"(#ideas)"`, while preserving the existing behavior for plain text (no tags) and multi-tag notes like `"hello #world #swift"`.

Verified all four cases:
- `"shopping list,#urgent."` → `["#urgent"]`
- `"(#ideas)"` → `["#ideas"]`
- `"hello #world #swift"` → `["#world", "#swift"]`
- `"just plain text"` → `[]`

No existing tests were broken (the only test in the suite is `extractTagsSimple`, which still passes with the new implementation).


